  {:namespace "day8.re-frame2-xray.core", :var "close!", :tier :tooling, :kind :fn, :owner "tools/xray", :status "post-v1 lib", :facade? true, :runtime-verified? true, :action :keep, :justification "Front porch: the visibility half of the open! / close! pair Conventions §Lifecycle-verb law names -- close! hides an already-mounted shell and leaves it re-open!-able, which is why it is NOT unmount! or destroy-*. Splitting it from open! would split one two-call workflow across two requires."}
  {:namespace "day8.re-frame2-xray.core", :var "configure!", :tier :tooling, :kind :fn, :owner "tools/xray", :status "post-v1 lib", :facade? true, :runtime-verified? true, :action :keep, :justification "Front porch, and named by Conventions §Lifecycle-verb law on THIS facade specifically -- configure! is the config-mutation verb across re-frame.core, re-frame.story and day8.re-frame2-xray.core alike. It is also the entry point the boot order is written around: requiring the facade is side-effect-free (rf2-5w06uu), so a host calls configure! and only then init!, which is what lets :rf.xray/auto-open? false win deterministically before any auto-open."}
  {:namespace "day8.re-frame2-xray.core", :var "focus!", :tier :tooling, :kind :fn, :owner "tools/xray", :status "post-v1 lib", :facade? true, :runtime-verified? true, :action :keep, :justification "An explicitly-recorded deliberate single-import re-export, which is the exception Conventions §Facade policy provides for: tools/xray/spec/API.md §Wider public surface rows it in the focus namespace as `focus! (the entry point, re-exported through core)`. The owning namespace day8.re-frame2-xray.focus keeps the command shape, the ownership boundary and the pure translation fn; the facade carries only the host-facing door, because the host sending the command is Story, not Xray. Contract at 008-Embedding-Contract §Host-facing focus API."}
  {:namespace "day8.re-frame2-xray.core", :var "init!", :tier :tooling, :kind :fn, :owner "tools/xray", :status "post-v1 lib", :facade? true, :runtime-verified? true, :action :keep, :justification "Front porch for a tooling product: the manual-install entry point, and one of exactly two install paths a host chooses between (the other is wiring day8.re-frame2-xray.preload into :devtools/preloads). tools/xray/spec/API.md §Canonical documents it first and rf2-g2a5v fixes its role against configure! and persisted Settings -- configure! is static boot config, init! the lifecycle hook that receives the merged config. A host that requires the facade at all requires it for this."}
  {:namespace "day8.re-frame2-xray.core", :var "load-theme", :tier :tooling, :kind :fn, :owner "tools/xray", :status "post-v1 lib", :facade? true, :runtime-verified? true, :action :keep, :justification "PLACEMENT is settled and is what this axis records: tools/xray/spec/API.md §Canonical rows it, and editor-driven palette sync is an ordinary host workflow reached in one call, so it stays on the facade. SPELLING IS LEFT FOR AN OPERATOR RULING and is deliberately NOT recorded as :rename. This is the one export here that mutates without a bang -- it installs a <style> override into <head> through global-styles/set-host-theme-css!, which does carry one -- and Conventions §Naming bucket 3 would bang it. But `load-*` appears on NO row of the closed lifecycle-verb roster, and §Lifecycle-verb law states that adding a verb to that table is a Spec change rather than a per-author call, so the repair is genuinely ambiguous between load-theme! and a roster row for load-*. Recorded keep with the uncertainty stated, per the CONTESTED clause; a rename after the first external alpha would be a consumer-visible break, which is why it is raised now rather than assumed."}
  {:namespace "day8.re-frame2-xray.core", :var "open!", :tier :tooling, :kind :fn, :owner "tools/xray", :status "post-v1 lib", :facade? true, :runtime-verified? true, :action :keep, :justification "Front porch: the default true-inline mount, and by tools/xray/spec/API.md §open! / open-overlay! / popout! what 95% of host code reaches for. Conventions §Lifecycle-verb law rows open! / close! as the visibility pair, so the spelling is the law's own. Also one of the six verbs the preload mirrors onto window.day8.re_frame2_xray, which keeps the CLJS and JS-console vocabularies identical."}
  {:namespace "day8.re-frame2-xray.core", :var "open-overlay!", :tier :tooling, :kind :fn, :owner "tools/xray", :status "post-v1 lib", :facade? true, :runtime-verified? true, :action :keep, :justification "Names a DISTINCT mount surface, not a mode of open!: the transient ESC-closeable overlay that floats above the host instead of participating in its layout. rf2-sa4fr ruled the rename question explicitly -- a mode-symmetric triplet (open-inline! / open-overlay! / open-popout!) was considered and REFUSED because the three verbs name kinds of mount, and flattening them would cost the rank signal that bare open! is the default. That standing ruling is why no :rename is recorded here."}
  {:namespace "day8.re-frame2-xray.core", :var "popout!", :tier :tooling, :kind :fn, :owner "tools/xray", :status "post-v1 lib", :facade? true, :runtime-verified? true, :action :keep, :justification "Names a DISTINCT mount surface: the same-browser second window, where the shell gets its own document context, React root, theme cascade and keybinding. Covered by the same rf2-sa4fr ruling as open-overlay!, and by 017-Test-Coverage-Matrix as a shipped host-facing launch mode."}
  {:namespace "day8.re-frame2-xray.core", :var "set-auto-open!", :tier :tooling, :kind :fn, :owner "tools/xray", :status "post-v1 lib", :facade? true, :runtime-verified? true, :action :keep, :justification "One of exactly four per-key setters tools/xray/spec/API.md §Wider public surface names as deliberately re-exported so common boot wiring lands in one require -- and the same section names the setters deliberately NOT re-exported (set-project-root!, set-keybinding-enabled!, set-filter-seed! and the rest, which hosts reach through day8.re-frame2-xray.config). The porch/workshop line this audit exists to draw is therefore already drawn and documented for this family, and this var is on the porch side of it: suppressing auto-open is boot-time wiring almost every embedding host does."}
  {:namespace "day8.re-frame2-xray.core", :var "set-editor!", :tier :tooling, :kind :fn, :owner "tools/xray", :status "post-v1 lib", :facade? true, :runtime-verified? true, :action :keep, :justification "One of the four highest-traffic setters §Wider public surface re-exports by name. It backs the Open-in-editor affordance, which is per-developer configuration nearly every host sets once at boot, and its accepted values (:vscode / :cursor / :windsurf / :zed / :idea / {:custom <uri-template>}) are the ones a reader most often wants beside init!."}
  {:namespace "day8.re-frame2-xray.core", :var "set-egress-profile!", :tier :tooling, :kind :fn, :owner "tools/xray", :status "post-v1 lib", :facade? true, :runtime-verified? true, :action :keep, :justification "One of the four highest-traffic setters §Wider public surface re-exports by name, and the one with the strongest reason to be legible from the facade: it selects the EP-0015 per-(tool,frame) reveal grain, where :rf.egress/local-redacted is the default and :rf.egress/local-raw is the trusted-local operator opt-in that reveals sensitive AND large values verbatim. A privacy opt-in belongs where a reviewer will see it, not behind a subnamespace door."}
  {:namespace "day8.re-frame2-xray.core", :var "set-target-frame!", :tier :tooling, :kind :fn, :owner "tools/xray", :status "post-v1 lib", :facade? true, :runtime-verified? true, :action :keep, :justification "Front porch: the write half of the pair above, and the surface a host with several frames needs on its first afternoon. Named parallel to the :rf.xray/target-frame sub and :rf.xray/set-target-frame event it drives, so the facade spelling matches runtime reality. Banged per Conventions §Naming bucket 3 -- it mutates Xray's own :rf/xray frame."}
  {:namespace "day8.re-frame2-xray.core", :var "status", :tier :tooling, :kind :fn, :owner "tools/xray", :status "post-v1 lib", :facade? true, :runtime-verified? true, :action :keep, :justification "Front porch, and the FIRST call a host makes when Xray does not appear: it returns the mount/API state including the last non-blocking diagnostic for a missing [data-rf-xray-host] layout host. tools/xray/spec/API.md §Wider public surface rows it among the six browser globals the preload installs, so the console recovery path and the CLJS one are the same var. A read, hence no bang."}
  {:namespace "day8.re-frame2-xray.core", :var "target-frame", :tier :tooling, :kind :fn, :owner "tools/xray", :status "post-v1 lib", :facade? true, :runtime-verified? true, :action :keep, :justification "Front porch: the one-shot read of which HOST frame Xray is inspecting -- the read half of the frame-picker pair, returning nil for UNSELECTED because EP-0002 (rf2-bd4div) removed the :rf/default absence-repair fallback. Reactive consumers subscribe to :rf.xray/target-frame directly, so this var exists precisely for the non-reactive host call the facade is for."}
